BOXBEG
<b>A Little Give and Take</b>
BOXMID
To date, I have received a couple of emails from people starting
up classes based on the book (even a high school class---very cool).
Would you like to exchange ideas for class activities,
projects, lectures, and experiments?  If so, this is the place to do
it.  Send me <a
href="mailto:gary.flake@usa.net">email</a> with any questions that
your have, or with resources that you want to share.

<p>
Possible contributions could be:
<ul>
<li>   lecture transparencies in power-point, PS, or PDF,
<li>   a compilation of student project ideas,
<li>   problem sets and solutions within specific areas,
<li>   quizzes, tests, homework or program assignments,
<li>   actual student projects, or
<li>   source code for new and improved examples.                   
</ul>

<p>
So, in a nutshell, if you have something to contribute, <a
href="mailto:gary.flake@usa.net">send it to me</a>.
If you need something and want to post a request, <a
href="mailto:gary.flake@usa.net">send that as well</a>. 

<p>This page will have a download section for class / instructor
resources as soon as critical mass on contributions is achieved,
BOXEND

<p>
BOXBEG
<b>Recent <i>CBofN</i> Sightings</b>
BOXMID
The following is a partial list of classes that use (or have used)
<i>CBofN</i>.

<ul> 

<li>
<a href="http://www.cs.unm.edu/~forrest/">Stephanie Forrest</a> of the
<a href="http://www.unm.edu/">University of New Mexico</a> is teaching
Topics in Complex Adaptive Systems with <i>CBofN</i>.
<br><br>


<li>
<a href="http://www.usc.edu/dept/LAS/ir/faculty/tr-alker.htm">Hayward
Alker</a> of the <a href="http://www.usc.edu/">University of Southern
California</a> taught an advanced International Relations course based
on <i>CBofN</i>.
<br><br>


<li> <a href="http://www.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/lmi/mschmitt/">Michael
Schmitt</a> of Ruhr-Universit&auml;t Bochum teaches <a
href="http://www.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/ffm/sommer/300.htm">Algorithmic
Description of Complex Systems</a> and uses <i>CBofN</i> as the
primary text.
<br><br>


<li>
<a href="http://snyflcaa.fingerlakes.edu/~SAMANTPG/">Sam Samanta</a> of
<a href="http://www.fingerlakes.edu/">Finger Lakes Community College</a> uses
